        <div class="canvas-body">
          <p class="canvas-intro">Mountains is a luxury technology house — a fund and a studio for an industry worth five point eight trillion dollars that runs almost entirely on software built for somebody else.</p>
          <p class="canvas-para">Placeholder copy. The identity derives from one painting: a Payne's indigo massif whose shadows are not drawn but computed, from surface orientation against a travelling sun, then quantised into coarse wash bands. Sun-facing facets are unpainted paper — never lit, simply not covered.</p>
          <p class="canvas-para">The mark follows the same logic. The studio asterisk is folded over its twenty-four-fold symmetry and quantised to an eleven-by-eleven field, at which point the twelve rays collapse into a plain diamond of twenty-five cells.</p>
